This Service Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into between Columbus Home Solutions, LLC ("Contractor") and the Client named above for the construction and/or remodeling work described in the attached Estimate and Scope of Work.

## **1. Scope of Work**

Contractor will perform the work as described in the project estimate and scope of work attached to this Agreement. The scope of work is incorporated by reference as part of this Agreement. Any work not explicitly described in the scope of work is not included in the contract price.

## **2. Communication**

Contractor will keep Client informed of project progress through regular updates via phone, text, email, or the Client Project Portal. Client will have access to a secure online portal where they can view project photos, schedule, invoices, documents, and communicate directly with Contractor.

Primary point of contact: Tony Columbus, **{{company_phone}}**, **{{company_email}}**

## **3. Project Timeline**

Work will begin on or about **{{start_date}}** with an estimated completion date of **{{target_end_date}}**. Scheduling changes will be communicated as needed. Timeline may be affected by weather, material availability, permitting, inspections, change orders, or other factors outside of Contractor's reasonable control.

## **4. Payment Terms**

The total contract price is **{{contract_total}}**, payable according to the following schedule:

**{{payment_schedule}}**

All invoices are due within seven (7) days of receipt. Payments may be made by check (no additional fee) or by credit card or ACH bank transfer (a 3.5% convenience fee applies to all electronic payments). This fee covers payment processing costs and will be clearly disclosed on each invoice.

## **5. Late Payment Fee**

A late fee of $50.00 per day will be added to any invoice not paid within seven (7) days of receipt. Contractor reserves the right to suspend work if payment is more than fourteen (14) days past due. Work will resume once all outstanding balances and accrued late fees are paid in full.

## **6. Price Escalation**

The contract price has been calculated based on current prices for building materials. Should there be an increase in the cost of specified materials after execution of this Agreement, Contractor will notify Client in writing with documentation of the price increase. Client agrees to pay the verified cost increase. If a material price increase would cause the total contract price to increase by more than ten percent (10%), Contractor will provide written notice before purchasing additional materials, and Client may choose to approve the increase, select alternative materials, or modify the scope of work.

## **7. Change Orders**

Any changes to the agreed scope of work must be documented in a written Change Order, which will describe the modified work, the cost impact (addition or credit), and any effect on the project timeline. Change Orders require Client signature before work proceeds. Approved Change Orders become part of this Agreement and adjust the contract total accordingly. Client understands that change orders may affect the project timeline.

## **8. Warranty**

Contractor provides a one-year workmanship warranty on all completed work, beginning on the date of project completion. This warranty covers defects in workmanship and does not cover normal wear and tear, damage caused by Client or third parties, issues resulting from improper maintenance, or defects in materials covered by manufacturer warranties. If a warranty claim arises, Client should contact Contractor promptly. Contractor will inspect the issue and perform repairs at no cost if the claim is covered under this warranty.

## **9. Insurance ****&**** Licensing**

Columbus Home Solutions, LLC is licensed and insured in the State of Arkansas. Contractor maintains general liability insurance and workers compensation coverage. Certificates of insurance are available upon request.

## **10. Site Access ****&**** Working Hours**

Client will provide Contractor and Contractor's subcontractors and suppliers reasonable access to the property during regular business hours (Monday through Friday, 7:00 AM to 7:00 PM) and at such other times as may be mutually agreed upon. Client is responsible for ensuring the work area is accessible and free of personal property that could be damaged during construction. Client is responsible for securing pets during working hours.

## **11. Permits ****&**** Inspections**

Contractor will obtain all necessary building permits and schedule all required inspections for work included in the scope of work. Permit fees are included in the contract price unless otherwise noted in the estimate. Client agrees to cooperate with inspection scheduling and provide access as needed.

## **12. Subcontractors**

Client acknowledges that some portions of the work may be performed by subcontractors who specialize in specific trades (electrical, plumbing, HVAC, concrete, etc.). These subcontractors are carefully selected based on skill, reliability, and quality of work. Contractor manages all subcontractor relationships and is responsible for the quality of their work under this Agreement.

## **13. Termination**

Either party may terminate this Agreement in writing. If Client terminates, Client will pay for all work completed through the termination date, all materials purchased or ordered, all subcontractor commitments made, and a termination fee equal to ten percent (10%) of the remaining contract balance. If Contractor terminates due to non-payment or breach by Client, Client will pay for all completed work, materials, and outstanding balances immediately.

## **14. Dispute Resolution**

The parties agree to resolve any disputes arising from this Agreement first by good faith negotiation. If the dispute cannot be resolved through negotiation within thirty (30) days, the parties agree to submit the dispute to mediation before pursuing any legal action. This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Arkansas.

## **15. Entire Agreement**

This Agreement, together with the attached Estimate, Scope of Work, and any executed Change Orders, constitutes the entire agreement between the parties. No verbal agreements or representations are binding unless incorporated into this Agreement in writing.

**By signing below (in person or electronically), both parties acknowledge that they have read, understand, and agree to all terms stated in this document. Electronic signatures are legally binding and carry the same weight as handwritten signatures under federal and Arkansas law.**

